+	/* This means that the cleanup function was called, so the cancel
+	 * request was honored during sem_wait() inside pthread_mutex_lock().
+	 *
+	 * When CONFIG_PTHREAD_MUTEX_UNSAFE is defined, pthread_mutex_lock() is
+	 * implemented using sem_wait(), which is a POSIX cancellation point.
+	 * The cancellation is acted upon during sem_wait(), causing the cleanup
+	 * handler to execute (cleanup_flag = -1). This is POSIX-compliant
+	 * behavior, so the test passes.
+	 *
+	 * When CONFIG_PTHREAD_MUTEX_UNSAFE is NOT defined, the mutex
